  "id": "theascensiongate",
  "note": "The one building in Coldwater with a HOLE in it. It is a gate and it was a solid block, which is the single most literal way a silhouette can be wrong — you cannot pass through the thing the whole quarter is named for walking through. Two piers carry a lintel now, so the opening is real geometry rather than something a description asks you to imagine. ⚠ THE GAP IS REAL TO EVERYTHING DOWNSTREAM, which is the point and also the thing to check before moving it: the mass primitives are what `modelSolid` builds CFIT collision from, what the truck ground probe reads and what the occluder hulls are cut from, so an aircraft can fly between the piers and a shadow falls in two pieces. Both piers are unyawed boxes, which is what lets the louvre banks and the lintel sign be bolted to something. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the asc_gate arm back.",
